From 34c44ff646018fbf8dac5a9f325274e0ab1448c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:26:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 102/114] core: restore the public atom driver registration API

Plugins written against oFono 1.x register atom drivers by calling
ofono_<type>_driver_register(), taking the driver name from the struct's
name field. oFono 2.x removed both the field and the functions, leaving
external plugins no way to supply a driver.

Restore them for every atom type on top of the runtime registry, so
out-of-tree plugins such as ofono-binder-plugin build and work unmodified.
The name field is added as the first struct member, matching the layout
those plugins were written against; builtin drivers do not set it and are
unaffected.

sim keeps Sailfish's versioned variant: the public register macro passes
OFONO_SIM_DRIVER_API_VERSION so a rebuild automatically opts into the
current struct layout, while the plain function remains for binaries
compiled before the macro existed. Upstream has no open_channel2 member,
which is what distinguished version 0 from version 1, so those cases
collapse into one.

(cherry picked from commit f568803cbaeec4a9561ee350a8f3297680102090)
Upstream-Status: Pending
